  "ArticleContents": "🔧 Poly Beats: Eclipse 0.10.2
More bug fixes, tending toward the themes side and some stuff relating to judgement and gameplay. Let's get it!

Changes
- You can now skip the fail animation via 'Skip Fail Animation' in Game settings. (Crafty)
- Moved 'Audio Sync Offset' setting over to the Audio menu.
- You can now use Themes you haven't uploaded to the Steam Workshop. (Crafty)
- 'Develop Themes' has been renamed to 'Local Themes' for easier finding. (Crafty)
- You can now set your local Themes inside the main Theme selector panel if you don't feel like messing with yours at that moment. (Crafty)
- If a map doesn't have note jump speed set, and it hasn't been set in map files - it will default to 12 unless you override it.

Bugs Fixed
- Fixed resolutions sometimes not applying once you set them. (Crafty)
- Fixed v-sync being enabled when not in fullscreen. (Crafty)
- Fixed fullscreen sometimes not applying, and not persisting between sessions. (Crafty)
- Fixed a bug where hold notes don't affect your accuracy. Again. How does this keep happening? (Crafty)
- Fixed a bug where hold notes double-incremented the combo count (Crafty)
- Fixed an issue on Galactic Warfare and PRIMAL RAGE where scores on those maps would not submit - yes, it was about spaces. (Crafty)
- Fixed a bug where it takes you to miss at least 2 notes for a combo streak to break. (Crafty)
- Fixed a bug where Atychiphobia charts just didn't work.
- Fixed a bug where hold note SFX can be heard before they spawn.

**Known Bugs**
- There's an issue with ANNIHILATION and the right side of tracks. Bare with.

GOOD PAN",
